      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "UNBRIDLED STORM (5) sets the standard after a Warwick Farm third in CG BM72 metro company, beaten a length and a half by Fierceness on soft ground. He now finds an easier race, draws barrier one and has Jason Collett taking over for Chris Waller. The profile is clean and progressive. SHOWMARA (4) brings the strongest winning record, having scored in BM68 grade at Hawkesbury after a narrow Nowra BM58 second, and Siena Grima's 1.5kg claim keeps him well placed at the weights. OKAMI STAR (8) has mixed recent figures, but the return to 1600m is significant given his two wins and four placings from 15 starts around the trip, along with a previous win at this track and distance. KINGSTON CHARM (3) at her top now fifth up and finds an easier contest. Never handled the soft (7) conditions when sixth over 1500m at Hawkesbury. Improver.",
